    "q-337856": {
      "dom_id": "step-q337856",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The function $\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1}$ is well defined for $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ and so to find this limit we substitute $x=2$ into the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1} & =\\sqrt{12\\cdot {2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
