      "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\sqrt{-3x+8}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{-3x+8}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253135/assets/267253d5390727373450d700edb503e595a8e8fe2bedda6ac93597a1dc9b3e9b.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty .\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
